#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Mga Benchmark {#benchmarks}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Published algorithmic "
"benchmarking](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.024034)"
" results demonstrate significant performance improvement across various "
"algorithms, including Bernstein-Vazirani, quantum Fourier transform, "
"Grover’s search, quantum approximate optimization algorithm, and variational"
" quantum eigensolver. The rest of this section provides more details about "
"types of algorithms you can run, as well as the expected performance and "
"runtimes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga resulta ng [nai-publish na algorithmic "
"benchmarking](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.024034)"
" ay nagpapakita ng makabuluhang pagpapabuti ng performance sa iba't ibang "
"algorithm, kabilang ang Bernstein-Vazirani, quantum Fourier transform, "
"Grover's search, quantum approximate optimization algorithm, at variational "
"quantum eigensolver. Ang natitirang bahagi ng seksyong ito ay nagbibigay ng "
"karagdagang detalye tungkol sa mga uri ng algorithm na maaari mong "
"patakbuhin, pati na rin ang inaasahang performance at mga runtime.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following independent studies demonstrate how Q-CTRL's Performance Management enables algorithmic research at record-breaking scale:\n"
"- [Parametrized Energy-Efficient Quantum Kernels for Network Service Fault Diagnosis](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.09724v1) - up to 50-qubit quantum kernel learning\n"
"- [Tensor-based quantum phase difference estimation for large-scale demonstration](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.04946) - up to 33-qubit quantum phase estimation\n"
"- [Hierarchical Learning for Quantum ML: Novel Training Technique for Large-Scale Variational Quantum Circuits](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.12929) - up to 21-qubit quantum data loading\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga sumusunod na independyenteng pag-aaral ay nagpapakita kung paano pinapagana ng Performance Management ng Q-CTRL ang algorithmic na pananaliksik sa record-breaking na sukat:\n"
"- [Parametrized Energy-Efficient Quantum Kernels for Network Service Fault Diagnosis](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.09724v1) - hanggang 50-qubit quantum kernel learning\n"
"- [Tensor-based quantum phase difference estimation for large-scale demonstration](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.04946) - hanggang 33-qubit quantum phase estimation\n"
"- [Hierarchical Learning for Quantum ML: Novel Training Technique for Large-Scale Variational Quantum Circuits](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.12929) - hanggang 21-qubit quantum data loading\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following table provides a rough guide on accuracy and runtimes from "
"prior benchmarking runs on `ibm_fez`. Performance on other devices may vary."
" The usage time is based on an assumption of 10,000 shots per circuit. The "
"\"Number of qubits\" indicated is not a hard limitation but represents rough"
" thresholds where you can expect extremely consistent solution accuracy. "
"Larger problem sizes have been successfully solved, and testing beyond these"
" limits is encouraged.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na talahanayan ay nagbibigay ng magaspang na gabay sa "
"katumpakan at mga runtime mula sa mga nakaraang benchmarking run sa "
"`ibm_fez`. Ang performance sa ibang device ay maaaring magkaiba. Ang oras ng"
" paggamit ay batay sa assumption na 10,000 shot bawat circuit. Ang \"Bilang "
"ng mga qubit\" na ipinahiwatig ay hindi isang mahigpit na limitasyon kundi "
"kumakatawan sa tantiyang mga threshold kung saan maaari kang umasa ng "
"napaka-consistent na katumpakan ng solusyon. Matagumpay na nalutas ang mas "
"malalaking sukat ng problema, at hinihikayat ang pagsubok na higit pa sa mga"
" limitasyong ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example    | Number of qubits | Accuracy | Measure of accuracy | Total time (s) | Runtime usage (s) | Primitive (Mode) |\n"
"| ---------  | ---------------- | -------------------------- | -------- | ---------- | ------------- |------------- |\n"
"| Bernstein–Vazirani  |  50Q    | 100%  | Success Rate (Percentage of runs where the correct answer is the highest count bitstring)     | 10    | 8         | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum Fourier Transform | 30Q              | 100% | Success Rate (Percentage of runs where the correct answer is the highest count bitstring)      | 10    | 8        | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum Phase Estimation  | 30Q   | 99.9998%  | Accuracy of the angle found: `1- abs(real_angle - angle_found)/pi`  | 10  | 8  | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum simulation: Ising model (15 steps) | 20Q  | 99.775%   |  $A$ (defined below)  |  60 (per step)  | 15 (per step)   | Estimator |\n"
"| Quantum simulation 2: molecular dynamics (20 time points) | 34Q  |  96.78%  |  $A_{mean}$ (defined below)   | 10 (per time point)    | 6 (per time point)  | Estimator |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Halimbawa    | Bilang ng qubit | Katumpakan | Sukatan ng katumpakan | Kabuuang oras (s) | Paggamit ng runtime (s) | Primitive (Mode) |\n"
"| ---------  | ---------------- | -------------------------- | -------- | ---------- | ------------- |------------- |\n"
"| Bernstein–Vazirani  |  50Q    | 100%  | Success Rate (Porsyento ng mga run kung saan ang tamang sagot ang bitstring na may pinakamataas na bilang)     | 10    | 8         | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum Fourier Transform | 30Q              | 100% | Success Rate (Porsyento ng mga run kung saan ang tamang sagot ang bitstring na may pinakamataas na bilang)      | 10    | 8        | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum Phase Estimation  | 30Q   | 99.9998%  | Katumpakan ng nahanap na anggulo: `1- abs(real_angle - angle_found)/pi`  | 10  | 8  | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum simulation: Ising model (15 hakbang) | 20Q  | 99.775%   |  $A$ (tinukoy sa ibaba)  |  60 (bawat hakbang)  | 15 (bawat hakbang)   | Estimator |\n"
"| Quantum simulation 2: molecular dynamics (20 time point) | 34Q  |  96.78%  |  $A_{mean}$ (tinukoy sa ibaba)   | 10 (bawat time point)    | 6 (bawat time point)  | Estimator |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Defining the accuracy of the measurement of an expectation value - the metric $A$ is defined as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"A = 1 - \\frac{|\\epsilon^{ideal} - \\epsilon^{meas}|}{\\epsilon^{ideal}_{max} - \\epsilon^{ideal}_{min}},\n"
"$$\n"
"where $ \\epsilon^{ideal} $ = ideal expectation value,  $ \\epsilon^{meas} $ = measured expectation value, $\\epsilon^{ideal}_{max} $ = ideal maximum value, and $\\epsilon^{ideal}_{min}$ = ideal minimum value. $A_{mean}$ is simply the average of the value of $A$ across multiple measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagtukoy ng katumpakan ng pagsukat ng expectation value — ang metric na $A$ ay tinukoy tulad ng sumusunod:\n"
"$$\n"
"A = 1 - \\frac{|\\epsilon^{ideal} - \\epsilon^{meas}|}{\\epsilon^{ideal}_{max} - \\epsilon^{ideal}_{min}},\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang $ \\epsilon^{ideal} $ = ideal na expectation value, $ \\epsilon^{meas} $ = nasukat na expectation value, $\\epsilon^{ideal}_{max} $ = ideal na maximum value, at $\\epsilon^{ideal}_{min}$ = ideal na minimum value. Ang $A_{mean}$ ay simpleng average ng halaga ng $A$ sa maraming pagsukat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This metric is used because it is invariant to global shifts and scaling in "
"the range of attainable values. In other words, regardless of whether you "
"shift the range of possible expectation values higher or lower or increase "
"the spread, the value of $A$ should remain consistent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagamit ang metric na ito dahil ito ay invariant sa mga global shift at "
"scaling sa hanay ng mga maaabot na halaga. Sa madaling salita, anuman ang "
"itaas o ibaba mo ang hanay ng mga posibleng expectation value o palawakin "
"ang pagkakalat, dapat manatiling consistent ang halaga ng $A$.\n"

